LRC14 oriented-tope / boundary-cocircuit proof pass (codex S164)
======================================================================

Method
------
Cut R/Z by all endpoints (14k +/- 1)/(14v).
Open cells are topes; boundary endpoints are possible cocircuits.
open all-safe tope: an interval where every speed is lonely.
boundary cocircuit: an endpoint where every speed is non-dangerous, with at least one equality owner.
forbidden wall candidate: no open all-safe tope and no boundary cocircuit.

