  boundary_cocircuit_atom > endpoint_arrangement_sheaf > owner_sum_zero_wall > open_all_safe_tope > cyclic_tope_morse_graph > moment_dual_shadow > raw_residue_tournament

Readout
-------
1. AP and GW are not open topes; they are boundary-cocircuit atoms.
2. Every audited named non-AP/GW hard row has an open all-safe tope.
3. In the one-swap hard bank, forbidden wall candidates are absent.
4. A strict LRC14 counterexample must therefore be a no-tope/no-cocircuit wall packet.
5. Candidate theorem: every no-tope/no-cocircuit wall packet constructs a K33/H=7 state lift or contradicts endpoint-owner parity.
